    q1: {
      label: 'Assessment & Plan',
      answer: '{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"She came to Singapore on 2/1/25 and was fine but started coughing last night and felt slightly wheezy. She had asthma on Ventolin inhaler and had 6 puffs from last night to this am. She remained somewhat SOB and some chest discomfort and thought she was having GERD. She decided to come here and was found to have a low spo2 of 93%. No severe chest pain and no gastric pain. No fever. She had some sashimi last night and took some fish this am but no known allergy to any of this food. "}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Clinically she had appeared slightly dyspneic and felt better after the Neb ("},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Ventolin(1ml)/Pulmicort(2ml)/Atrovent(8drops)/NACL(1ml)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"(SPO2 improved to 100% post neb)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"FBC/CRP/MYCOPLASMA IgM/TROP-T, PROBNP, CKMB..raised PROBNP 188 and CRP30"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"ECG: NSR, T INVERSION IN LEADS III, AVF, V2,3 ? ANT INFARCT, poor R wave progression in precordial leads"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"FLU A/B.ART: ALL NEG,"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"underline"}],"text":"PATIENT ADVISED TO GO TO UCC FPH TO SEE DR DEVINER SINGH BUT PATIENT WANTED TO RETURN HOME 1ST AND ADVISED BEST TO GO TO A&E AT THE EARLIEST SYMPTOMS FOR A REVIEW OF HER RESULTS AND ECG AND FURTHER TESTS. PATIENT NOTED THE SYMPTOMS TO LOOK OUT FOR."}]},{"type":"paragraph"}]}',
